<p>Benin held a presidential election on April 12 to choose a successor to President Patrice Talon, who is stepping down after serving two five-year terms. Finance Minister Romuald Wadagni, backed by Talon, was widely seen as the favorite, while FCBE candidate Paul Hounkpè was the only other name on the ballot. The vote offers a clear moment of constitutional transition in Benin after a decade under Talon, but it also unfolded amid criticism over the narrow field of candidates and limits on dissent. With only two candidates competing and reports highlighting pressure on critics, the election has been framed both as an orderly handover of power and as a test of the country’s political openness.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/nB5quxplUNT8wQwWgN8qMfAq7D9mLlqhqhIKxL9xmOKuUm38RuKvtx3T_cjphzCcyghO5r8FJBFNQkJ0N7FnsHZK-gsJ9gAbh5Y9vnPS3ToCHl-WCV82SKOpG5IR7uoYFITW-7T8TCUbl9FUy1DqC2AAD7CepRTqZr5yLCuq8w' alt='Voters take part in Benin&#x27;s presidential election to choose a successor to Patrice Talon.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Profile gap: DW reported via AllAfrica that Hounkpè entered the race with a much lower public profile than Wadagni.</li><li>Limited change expectations: RFI said the political climate around the vote reduced expectations for a major shift regardless of the election result.</li><li>Polls close: Al Jazeera reported that polling stations closed on Sunday after nationwide voting, with Wadagni still expected to win as counting began.</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/benin-votes-new-president-finance-minister-favored-succeed-131965900'>Benin holds presidential election with finance minister favored to succeed Talon</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://allafrica.com/stories/202604130100.html'>Benin: Benin Election - Finance Minister Wadagni Expected to Win</a> - allafrica.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/4/12/polls-close-in-benin-with-finance-minister-expected-to-win-election'>Polls close in Benin with finance minister expected to win election</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.reuters.com/world/africa/benin-finance-minister-expected-coast-presidential-election-win-2026-04-12/'>Beninese citizens vote to elect a president that will succeed the incumbent Patrice Talon and serve for the next seven years. Finance minister Romuald Wadagni and FCBE candidate Paul Hounkpè are the only two candidates on the ballot.</a> - reuters.com</li></ul>